<h1>AI-powered RFP &amp; Proposal Pipeline</h1>
<p class="lede">An end-to-end workflow designed to improve how opportunities are found, assessed, matched and turned into proposals.</p>
<div class="article-content">
<h2>The problem</h2>
<p>RFP and funding opportunities can arrive through multiple channels and require rapid assessment against organisational capabilities, partners, geography and programme priorities. The challenge was to turn a largely manual opportunity process into a structured workflow.</p>
<h2>The workflow</h2>
<p>The pipeline brings together opportunity ingestion, AI categorisation, partner matching, storage, bid/no-bid scoring and proposal generation.</p>
<div class="pipeline"><div class="pipe"><span>01</span>Opportunity ingestion</div><div class="pipe"><span>02</span>AI categorisation</div><div class="pipe"><span>03</span>Partner matching</div><div class="pipe"><span>04</span>Bid / no-bid scoring</div><div class="pipe"><span>05</span>Proposal generation</div></div>
<h2>My role</h2>
<p>The work combines programme management with technology and AI workflow design: defining the process, structuring information, identifying where AI can reduce repetitive work, and connecting the workflow to practical proposal decisions.</p>
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p>The significance is not AI for its own sake. The objective is a repeatable operating process that helps a programme organisation identify relevant opportunities, make better-informed decisions and move efficiently from an opportunity to a potential response.</p>
</div>
</article>
